=== pycubrid.aio Async CRUD Demo ===

[setup] Created cookbook_async_demo
[1] Inserted 4 rows asynchronously

[2] All rows (fetchall):
    id=1  name=alice  score=90
    id=3  name=carol  score=88
    id=2  name=bob  score=75
    id=4  name=dave  score=60

[3] First row (fetchone):
    name=alice  score=90

[4] Updated alice's score to 100

--- async API summary ---
  await pycubrid.aio.connect(**DB_CONFIG)        -> AsyncConnection
  conn.cursor()                                   -> AsyncCursor (no await)
  await cur.execute(sql, params)                  -> AsyncCursor
  await cur.executemany(sql, params_list)         -> AsyncCursor
  await cur.fetchone() / fetchall() / fetchmany() -> rows
  await conn.commit() / conn.rollback()
  await conn.close()

See also: 02_async_sqlalchemy.py for the SQLAlchemy async engine.
